# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CTP planner -- what must never enter the repository, and why.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# RAW MES HISTORY (~4.4 GB, 32 M rows). These are the plant's production event
# logs. They are the input to L0-L2 mining only; every mined artefact the
# scheduler needs is committed under warehouse/derived/ and INPUT/derived/.
curing/
o_production/
io_production_consumption/
bom_pcr_tbr/
Sku construction mapping/

# REGENERABLE WAREHOUSE PARTITIONS. `make ingest` rebuilds these from the raw
# CSVs. The three SMALL view directories the scheduler actually reads
# (derived/, params/, masters/, bom/, construction/, balance/) are committed --
# the three huge ones are not.
schedule/send/warehouse/building_output/
schedule/send/warehouse/consumption/
schedule/send/warehouse/curing/

# Virtualenv -- rebuild with the commands in README.md
.venv/
venv/

# RUN DIRECTORIES. One reference run per month is committed
# (schedule/send/runs/aug_ship and .../hz_ext72); everything else is a
# throwaway A/B arm and there have been hundreds.
schedule/send/runs/*
!schedule/send/runs/aug_ship/
!schedule/send/runs/hz_ext72/

# Export packs other than the two shipped ones.
schedule/send/output/*
!schedule/send/output/AUG2026_pack/
!schedule/send/output/JUL2026_pack/

# Excel lock files -- created whenever someone opens a workbook.
~$*
*.xlsx#
.~lock.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
